<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ardennes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ardennes is a region of wooded hills and plateaus spread across south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, Luxembourg and north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, with a fringe in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Thinly settled and long a frontier between French and German lands, it held medieval abbeys such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stavelot">Stavelot</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malmedy">Malmedy</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> German armies broke through it in 1940 and launched their last great offensive there in December 1944.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ardennes.jpg" alt="Ardennes" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pol GRANDMONT · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frahan_JPG01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Frederick’s house of <b>Ardennes</b> held Upper Lorraine for most of the next century, and Gothelo I briefly reunited both duchies between 1033 and 1044.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-lorraine">Duchy of Lorraine · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The last great German offensive in the <b>Ardennes</b> in December 1944 collapsed, and in 1945 Allied armies crossed the Rhine and the Oder.</blockquote><a href="/empire/nazi-germany">Nazi Germany · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>German forces attacked through the <b>Ardennes</b> in Belgium and Luxembourg, catching the Americans by surprise.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-16">16 December in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Allied forces restored their line in the <b>Ardennes</b>, ending Germany's last major offensive in the west.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-25">25 January in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The county emerged in the mid-10th century in the southern <b>Ardennes</b>, in the frontier region between the Lotharingian duchies and France.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-chiny">County of Chiny</a></li><li><blockquote>His descendants, and from 1136 the counts of Namur and later Limburg lines, expanded the county through the <b>Ardennes</b> and Moselle valley.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-luxembourg">County of Luxembourg</a></li></ul></section>
